{
  "comprehensible": "At the very last moment, he lost his nerve and betrayed his colleagues by shifting the blame onto them.",
  "glosses": [
    {
      "expression": "bottled it",
      "gloss": "lost his nerve and failed to do what he was supposed to do"
    },
    {
      "expression": "threw his colleagues under the bus",
      "gloss": "betrayed his colleagues or put them in trouble to protect himself"
    }
  ],
  "grammar": null,
  "translation": "彼は土壇場で怖じ気づき、同僚を犠牲にして自分を守った。"
}

{
  "comprehensible": "The house was in a condition of respectable, upper-class decline, because the people who lived there had moved away to mainland Europe a long time ago.",
  "glosses": [
    {
      "expression": "genteel decay",
      "gloss": "a state of decline that still keeps a respectable, upper-class appearance"
    },
    {
      "expression": "having long since repaired to",
      "gloss": "having moved to (a place) a long time ago; 'repaired to' is a formal, old-fashioned way of saying 'went to'"
    },
    {
      "expression": "the Continent",
      "gloss": "mainland Europe (used especially by British speakers)"
    }
  ],
  "grammar": "The phrase 'its occupants having long since repaired to the Continent' is a participle clause that gives the reason for the house's decay. It has no finite verb ('having repaired' is a participle), so it cannot stand alone as a sentence; it attaches to the main clause 'The house stood in a state of genteel decay' and explains why.",
  "translation": "その家は、上品な荒れ方をした状態で建っていた。住人たちはずっと前にヨーロッパ大陸へ移り住んでいたからだ。"
}

{
  "comprehensible": "The person renting the property must protect the owner from any claims that come from breaking any of the promises in this agreement.",
  "glosses": [
    {
      "expression": "indemnify",
      "gloss": "to protect someone from loss or damage by paying for it or taking legal responsibility"
    },
    {
      "expression": "lessee",
      "gloss": "the person who rents something (the tenant)"
    },
    {
      "expression": "lessor",
      "gloss": "the person who owns and rents out something (the landlord)"
    },
    {
      "expression": "covenants",
      "gloss": "formal promises or agreements, especially in a legal document"
    },
    {
      "expression": "herein",
      "gloss": "in this document"
    }
  ],
  "grammar": null,
  "translation": "賃借人は、本契約に定める約束の違反から生じるすべての請求に対して、賃貸人を補償しなければならない。"
}

{
  "comprehensible": "It is proper for us to think about whether acting in that way fits with what we are obliged to do.",
  "glosses": [
    {
      "expression": "behoves",
      "gloss": "is right or proper for (someone) to do"
    },
    {
      "expression": "such a course of action",
      "gloss": "that way of acting; that plan"
    },
    {
      "expression": "consonant with",
      "gloss": "in agreement with; consistent with"
    }
  ],
  "grammar": "The sentence uses a formal pattern: 'It behoves us to consider...' means 'It is proper for us to consider...'. The 'it' is a placeholder subject, and the real subject is the infinitive phrase 'to consider...'. The clause 'whether such a course of action is consonant with our obligations' is the object of 'consider'.",
  "translation": "そのような行動が我々の義務と一致するかどうかを考えることは、我々にとってふさわしいことである。"
}
